variable {R : Type u} {A : Type v} {Λ : Type w}
variable [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [CommRing Λ]
variable [Algebra R A] [Algebra R Λ] [Algebra A Λ] [IsScalarTower R A Λ]
variable {r : ℕ} (π : Fin r → R)

/-
Domain-style sampling for Lemma 16.9.2:
- primary domain: commutative algebra of finitely presented resolution factorizations, singular
  ideals, and reduction modulo the ideal generated by the eighth powers of a finite family;
- sampled owner declarations:
  `Ideal.torsionOf`,
  `RingHom.singularIdealIn`,
  `ResolvableAtPrime`,
  `Algebra.IsStrictlyStandard`,
  `Ideal.Quotient.algebraQuotientOfLEComap`,
  `Ideal.isPrime_map_quotientMk_of_isPrime`;
- best owner abstraction: the source-facing owner is `ResolvableAtPrime`, while the successive
  quotient torsion hypotheses should be stated through the chapter's canonical owner
  `Ideal.torsionOf`; the reduction data should stay as the canonical quotient ideal/image-of-prime
  constructions instead of parallel wrapper APIs;
- primitive data: the finitely presented factorization `A → B → Λ`, the singular-ideal
  containment/noncontainment conditions, the successive quotient torsion equalities for the family
  `π`, and the quotient ideal generated by the family `π i ^ 8`;
- derived API: the reduced prime `q / I8 Λ`, the quotient algebra structures on
  `R / I8`, `A / I8 A`, `Λ / I8 Λ`, and the reduction step in the main theorem.

Source/core/bridge triage:
- `source-facing`: `ResolvableAtPrime` and the lifting theorem
  `resolvableAtPrime_of_resolvableAtPrime_mod_piPowEight_family`;
- `core/canonical`: `Ideal.torsionOf`, `RingHom.singularIdealIn`,
  `Ideal.Quotient.algebraQuotientOfLEComap`, `Ideal.isPrime_map_quotientMk_of_isPrime`, and
